## Git & delivery of changes (IMPORTANT)
<!-- AUTOPILOT-INIT: fill in the real GitHub org/repo names and the PR base branch. -->
Work per-repo — only where you actually changed files.

**NEVER push directly to `main` or `develop`.** Default flow — feature branch + Pull Request:
1. `git fetch origin`
2. Base branch = `develop` if it exists on origin (`git ls-remote --heads origin develop` is non-empty), otherwise `main`.
3. Task branch: `git switch -c autopilot/<GID> origin/<base>` (if it already exists — `git switch autopilot/<GID>`). `<GID>` is the current task's gid.
4. Commit (message in English; the commit body MUST contain the Asana task permalink).
5. `git push -u origin autopilot/<GID>`
6. Open a Pull Request into the base branch:
   - if `gh` is available (`command -v gh` and it is authenticated): `gh pr create --base <base> --head autopilot/<GID> --title "<short>" --body "<what changed + Asana permalink>"` — keep the PR URL;
   - if `gh` is missing/unauthenticated: do NOT create a PR by hand — instead build the compare link `https://github.com/<org>/<repo>/compare/<base>...autopilot/<GID>?expand=1` so a human can open the PR from it.
7. Put the PR (or compare) URL into the Asana comment when moving the task to qa/done.

**Exception:** if the task EXPLICITLY says to push to `develop` or `main` directly, do what the task says (commit on that branch + `git push`, no PR).

**Interrupted session (WIP):** commit the leftovers on the task's FEATURE BRANCH and push that branch (`git push -u origin autopilot/<GID>`). Never push WIP to `main`/`develop`.

## Step 0 — Preparation
1. Read `autopilot/state/current-task.md` — it has everything for your task this session: GID, title, description, **subtasks**, real comments, the system event history, and linked tasks.
2. **Subtasks are part of the task.** Any subtask marked `⚠️ ОТКРЫТА И НАЗНАЧЕНА НА ТЕБЯ` is MANDATORY: the task is not done until every such subtask is implemented and closed with `asana complete <subtask_gid>`. Leave a detailed comment inside the subtask about what you did, and a short completion note in the parent task.
3. **If the task is in `reopen`:** the reason is in the open subtasks and in comments left AFTER the last move to reopen (system events in «История» are NOT comments and NOT the reopen reason; linked tasks are reference context only). If you cannot determine a concrete reason, do not guess — ask via the Blocked protocol.
4. **Attachments (screenshots etc.):** if `current-task.md` has a «Вложения» section (or the text has `get_asset?asset_id=NNN` links), download them with `asana download <gid>` and open the file with the Read tool — you can see images. For UI tasks the screenshot usually IS the spec.
5. Run `git status -sb` in the repositories you'll touch. If there are uncommitted changes from a previous killed session, commit them with the `WIP:` prefix **on the task's feature branch** per «Git & delivery of changes» (never push to main/develop). Do not revert or delete unfamiliar WIP commits.

## Step 1 — Work Execution
- Work iteratively: change → build/test → next step.
- Time-box is ~2.5 hours. If you run out of time, make a `WIP:` commit on the feature branch and push **the branch** (per «Git & delivery of changes»), describe the status in an Asana comment (in Russian, via the CLI), and end the session.

## Step 2 — Completion (FINAL)
- Before finishing, verify: **all subtasks assigned to the agent are done and closed** (`asana complete <gid>`). A task with open agent subtasks may NOT be moved to qa/done.
- Deliver changes per «Git & delivery of changes»: feature branch `autopilot/<GID>` → push branch → PR into the base branch, **unless the task explicitly says to push to develop/main directly**. Commit message in English; the commit body MUST include the **Asana task permalink**. Put the PR (or compare) URL into the Asana comment.
- **Where to move the task:**
  - **Can be tested manually (UI, flow):** create a testing subtask, then move to qa:
    ```
    asana subtask <gid> "Тестирование: <task_name>" --assignee operator --notes - <<'EOF'
    Нумерованные шаги ручной проверки и ожидаемые результаты (на русском).
    EOF
    asana qa <gid> - <<'EOF'
    Что сделано, хэши коммитов, ссылка на PR, как проверено, риски. План тестирования: см. сабтаску.
    EOF
    ```
  - **Purely internal changes (refactoring, CI):** `asana done <gid> "<Russian comment: what was done and why manual QA isn't needed>"`.
- Append the result to `autopilot/state/done.log` (time, GID, permalink, outcome).
- End the session.

## Blocked Protocol
Trigger this if the operator's intervention is required (access, decisions, payments) or the task/reopen reason is genuinely unclear.
1. Commit and push everything as `WIP:` on the feature branch.
2. `asana block <gid> - <<'EOF'` … `EOF` — comment (in Russian) with a clear list of required actions/questions; the command also reassigns to the operator and moves to blocked.
3. Append the task GID to `autopilot/state/blocked.txt`.
4. End the session.
